<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Zeelandia (Suriname)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Zeelandia is a fortress on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname-river">Suriname River</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paramaribo">Paramaribo</a>. Built by the English colonists of Willoughbyland, it was captured in February 1667 by a fleet from Zeeland under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-crijnssen">Abraham Crijnssen</a> and renamed after that province. It remained the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> military power in the colony, and in December 1982 it was the scene of the December murders, when fifteen critics of the military regime were killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-zeelandia-suriname.jpg" alt="Fort Zeelandia (Suriname)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Junie609 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Zeelandia_top_view_(photo_5)_located_at_Abraham_Crijnssenweg_1_paramaribo,_suriname.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
